# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps a host's live
# secrets and incident data from ever being baked into an image layer. If you
# already have a native install in this same folder, its config.json holds
# real tokens and server/data holds real tickets, cases and evidence - none
# of that belongs in an image that might end up pushed to a registry.
.git/
node_modules/

server/config.json
server/data/
server/service.json
deploy/config.json
deploy/data/

ui/index.html
dist/
aegis-v3.html
targets*.json
*.log
*.tmp
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
